oaxaca-desktop (4.0.6+git20261022.128.a95cf5f7-0oaxaca1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Based on Omarchy 4.0.6 instead of 4.0.4. From Omarchy's 4.0.5 and 4.0.6:
    - The screen lock decides each lock request from its current state, and
      recovers a stranded lock only when no other locker may hold it.
    - The bar starts faster, and a shell restart waits for the old shell
      to exit, so a restart no longer ends with no bar.
    - Links from every app open in the running default browser, and web
      apps hand their window to it, both faster than starting a browser.
    - On hybrid graphics, NVIDIA's video drivers are forced only when the
      NVIDIA GPU drives the display.
    - The calendar builds its month grid in UTC; an idle timeout of 0
      works; the monitor panel's display toggle is fixed; fastfetch labels
      swap correctly.
    - Audio: EasyEffects outputs and filter pairs resolve to the right
      sink, the speaker tuning asks RTKit for its priority directly, and
      the KEF LSX II LT USB speaker no longer suspends.
    - The shell's QML is ready for Qt 6.12.
  * Security: a factory reset now also replaces root's password hash and
    deletes the backups of the account files, which kept the previous
    owner's password hash.
  * Remove > Security > SSHD removes every standard SSH firewall rule, not
    only the rate limit on port 22.
  * Package names that start with a dash are never read as options by the
    package helpers.

 -- santisbon <santisbon@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:37:37 -0500

oaxaca-desktop (4.0.4+git20261022.127.788a310d-0oaxaca1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Security: a project's bin/ folder under ~/Work is no longer put on
    PATH. The first login wrote ~/Work/.mise.toml with mise's
    _.path = "{{ cwd }}/bin", so any repository cloned under ~/Work could
    supply commands. New users get no such file, and an update deletes the
    file when it is the unchanged one, or removes only that line from a
    file you edited, keeping a backup; mise's trust in the file is revoked
    either way. Run a project's own tools with an explicit path, such as
    ./bin/dev. From Omarchy 4.0.5 (commit 6ae40920).

