  * Installing software from the menu works on a system that has no
    package lists yet: oaxaca-pkg-add, which the Install entries use, runs
    apt-get update first when /var/lib/apt/lists holds none. A system
    installed by oaxaca-installer 0.1.11 had none until its first update,
    and Install > AI > Dictation failed with "Unable to locate package
    voxtype" (docs/7, choice 55).
  * No administrator password dialog when snapd starts: a udev rule in
    oaxaca-config hides snapd's start-up check image, a loop device backed
    by /tmp/syscheck-squashfs-*, from udisks2. The session's udiskie
    --automount tried to mount the image, and udisks2 asked for
    org.freedesktop.udisks2.filesystem-mount-system. Opening a menu starts
    snapd when snapd is idle, so the dialog could come up on any menu.

