oaxaca-desktop (4.0.6+git20261013-0oaxaca1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Version scheme: the upstream version is the Omarchy tag plus the date of
    the fork commit the packages are built from (+git<YYYYMMDD>), so every
    change to the fork has its own orig tarball; under the tag alone two
    revisions shared one orig tarball name with different contents.
  * New oaxaca-launch-dgpu: runs a command on the discrete GPU of a
    hybrid-graphics machine, through oaxaca-launch-nvidia on NVIDIA and
    with DRI_PRIME set to the AMD GPU's PCI address on AMD. The menu's
    launcher (oaxaca-launch-desktop) uses it for entries that ask for the
    discrete GPU and for applications listed in ~/.config/oaxaca/dgpu-apps
    (nvidia-apps, the list's first name, is still read), on NVIDIA and AMD
    machines alike. oaxaca-debug-launch shows the offload variables
    (docs/7 choice 43).
  * The port changes made since the first build, from the fork's branch
    (2026-10-10 to 2026-10-13): the Plymouth theme and its passphrase hint,
    the migrations runner, packages added to the base list (plymouth-label,
    pulseaudio-utils, gawk, libgtk-3-bin, thermald, intel-lpmd,
    lsp-plugins-lv2), the login screen's user fallback, mise for the
    commands that need it, the balanced default power profile, the
    installer's window rule, oaxaca-debug-launch, applications on the
    display GPU's Mesa driver on hybrid graphics with
    oaxaca-launch-nvidia, and the menu's discrete-GPU choice.

